<title>GERMANY: Quinn-benefits for Ireland in EMU even without UK.</title>
<headline>Quinn-benefits for Ireland in EMU even without UK.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1996-11-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Irish Finance Minister Ruairi Quinn said on Friday that the benefits of Ireland joining European Monetary Union without Britain outweighed the risks.</p>
<p>&quot;According to a number of studies we have had done, we believe the benefits for Ireland of being in EMU before the UK are greater than the potential risks,&quot; Quinn told Reuters Financial Television on the fringes of the banking congress being held in Frankfurt.</p>
<p>If Ireland joined first there would be a transition period before the UK joined EMU, but that would not pose great problems for Ireland, Quinn said.</p>
</text>
